I've made keywords for jboski and .camxes.. These are both online parsers,
otherwise known as grammar-check. They both support passing information via
web-link: .camxes.: pisu'o cevni cu prami re'e
ko<http://camxes.lojban.org/camxes/?text=pisu%27o%20cevni%20cu%20prami%20re%27e%20ko>jboski:
pisu'o
cevni cu prami re'e
ko<http://www.lojban.org/jboski/index.php?jbocku=pisu%27o%20cevni%20cu%20prami%20re%27e%20ko>

Neither of these have a search bar for them, however, so making a keyword
for them has to be done manually.

.camxes. -> "http://camxes.lojban.org/camxes/?text=%s"
jboski -> "http://www.lojban.org/jboski/index.php?jbocku=%s"

For example, this is the html export from my bookmarks on Firefox:

<DT><A HREF="http://camxes.lojban.org/camxes/?text=%s"
ADD_DATE="1329683038" LAST_MODIFIED="1329683302" SHORTCUTURL="cx">camxes</A>
<DT><A HREF="http://www.lojban.org/jboski/index.php?jbocku=%s"
ADD_DATE="1329683038" LAST_MODIFIED="1329683172" SHORTCUTURL="jb">jboski</A>

I don't know how to add terms for Chrome, but I'm sure one of you can
figure it out.

